{"shortDescription":"(TheNewswire)Victoria, British Columbia, Canada – TheNewswire - October 14, 2026 - Teuton Resources Corp.  (“Teuton” or “the Company”) (“TUO”-TSX-V) (\"TEUTF\"- OTCQB) is pleased to report the following exploration update from the Treaty Creek property: Joint Venture (“JV”) partner Tudor Gold Corp…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["(TheNewswire)"]},{"type":"p","children":["Victoria, British Columbia, Canada – TheNewswire - October 14, 2026 - Teuton Resources Corp.  (“Teuton” or “the Company”) (“TUO”-TSX-V) (\"TEUTF\"- OTCQB) is pleased to report the following exploration update from the Treaty Creek property: Joint Venture (“JV”) partner Tudor Gold Corp. (“Tudor”) has announced, in a news release dated October 14, 2026, results from a further four holes drilled at the PSP and PSE Zones. A third drill was recently added to the 2026 Treaty Creek program."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Tudor October 14, 2026 news release concerning Treaty Creek contains the following:"]},{"type":"p","children":["Drilling has expanded the recently discovered copper-gold-silver-molybdenum porphyry system (the “PSP Zone”) by cutting gold-dominant mineralization over 480 meters down-dip of previous drilling. Additionally, several higher-grade intercepts throughout the PSP Zone provided continuity between a high-grade gold-dominant overprint to the porphyry system akin to Tudor Gold’s Goldstorm Deposit located approximately one kilometer to the northeast. Near-surface gold-dominant mineralization in the low to intermediate sulfidation system (the “PSE Zone”) was extended along strike. Tudor expects to complete over 20,000 meters of drilling with three drill rigs to complete the remainder of the Exploration Program."]},{"type":"p","children":["Tudor has retained Fuse Advisors Inc. to prepare a Preliminary Economic Assessment examining the potential for an underground mining operation focused on the higher-grading gold mineralization at Treaty Creek’s Goldstorm Deposit outlined in the 2026 Mineral Resource estimate (“MRE”) for the Goldstorm Deposit (see Tudor’s news release dated January 22, 2026). The study is being finalized with results expected to be released in the coming weeks. Tudor’s 80%-owned Treaty Creek Project is located in the heart of the Golden Triangle of Northwestern British Columbia."]},{"type":"p","children":["See Table 1 below for select drill results of holes PS-26-29 to 32 accompanied by plan maps and cross sections."]},{"type":"p","children":["PSP Zone – Continued Expansion of the Porphyry System"]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole PS-26-30 intersected:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.85 g/t gold, and 2.94 g/t silver, over 96.30 meters starting 264.30 meters downhole, including"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["2.02 g/t gold, and 3.46 g/t silver, over 5.30 meters starting 265.50 meters downhole, and"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1.92 g/t gold, and 4.24 g/t silver, over 6.70 meters starting 297.80 meters downhole"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole PS-26-31 intersected:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1.16 g/t gold, 2.08 g/t silver, 0.21% copper and 116.91 ppm molybdenum over 11.00 meters starting 115.00 meters downhole"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.22 g/t gold, 1.42 g/t silver, 0.19% copper and25.10 ppm molybdenum, over 59.50 meters starting 141.00 meters downhole. including"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.44 g/t gold, 2.53 g/t silver, 0.36% copper and25.62 ppm molybdenum, over 18.00 meters starting 182.50 meters downhole"]}]}]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.67 g/t gold and 3.72 g/t silver over 37.50 meters starting 247.00 meters downhole, including"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1.20 g/t gold and13.41 g/t silver over 7.50 meters starting 277.00 meters downhole,"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole PS-26-32 intersected:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3.43 g/t gold, and 7.99 g/t silver, over 2.65 meters starting 267.35 meters downhole"]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["0.98 g/t gold, and 3.29 g/t silver, over 31.80 meters starting 646.90 meters downhole, including"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["3.98 g/t gold, and 14.72 g/t silver, over 4.20 meters starting 674.50 meters downhole"]}]}]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["15.05 g/t gold and5.33 g/t silver over 1.50 meters starting 913.50 meters downhole"]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Results from holes PS-26-30, PS-26-31, and PS-26-32, demonstrate consistent gold, silver, copper, and molybdenum values hosted within a potassic altered diorite (porphyry) intrusive.  Similar to the neighbouring Goldstorm Deposit, the newly discovered porphyry intrusive is located between higher-grade intervals of gold-dominant mineralization. Continued intercepts of higher-grade material demonstrate continuity of a high-grade gold-dominant overprint to the porphyry system. Drillhole PS-26-32, designed to test the down-dip continuity of the system, extended gold-dominant mineralization over 480 m down-dip from previous drilling while also intercepting several higher-grade, vein-hosted mineralized intervals shallower in the hole, opening a large target rich area throughout the greater Perfectstorm Zone area."]},{"type":"p","children":["The PSP Zone is located approximately one kilometer southwest of Treaty Creek’s Goldstorm Deposit at its closet point and four kilometers northeast of Seabridge Gold’s Iron Cap Deposit, along the northeast-southwest trending Sulphurets corridor that hosts multiple porphyry deposits and prospects.  The system now extends approximately 850 by 750 meters and remains open in all directions."]},{"type":"p","children":["PSE Zone – Broader Zones of Low to Intermediate Sulfidation Gold-dominant Mineralization"]},{"type":"p","children":["Hole PS-26-29 intersected:"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["1.16 g/t gold and 13.92 g/t silver over 25.50 metersstarting 238.50 meters downhole, including"]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["4.38 g/t gold and81.97 g/t silverover 3.00 metersstarting 240.00 meters downhole"]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Drillhole PS-26-20 intersected a continuance of near surface, gold-dominant vein-hosted mineralized system, adding to the volume of the previously identified mineralized system. Mineralization now occurs over an area of approximately 600 meters by 300m with a thickness varying between 25 meters up to over 100 meters."]},{"type":"p","children":["Three drills are now active at the Perfectstorm Zone and are focused on priority target areas identified by recent results."]},{"type":"p","children":["Table 1: Select Treaty Creek Drill Results"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":2},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Hole"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":2},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Collar Coords"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Dip/"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["From"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["To"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Interval"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Gold"]}]},{"